  "ate_describe": "ATE=6361.93, 90% interval [4490.15, 8233.7], n=12000; propensity range [0.002394, 0.9102].\nTarget: ATE over every row; 27.1% of rows have a cross-fitted propensity below 0.05 or above 0.95, where the outcome model is extrapolated and the estimate is sensitive to it. aipw(target='overlap') estimates the overlap-weighted effect instead.\nOutcome model: two-part (positive-outcome probability times the mean of the log outcome), chosen by outcome_model='auto' because the sparse-arm check flagged propensity bin(s) [0, 1], and the outcome is zero or positive with zeros, so the two-part model is used.\nPropensity: formula 'smooth+trees', chosen by propensity_learner='auto' on out-of-fold binomial deviance (0.927907 against 'smooth' 0.951295).\nAssumptions: consistency: each observed outcome equals the potential outcome under the observed treatment; conditional exchangeability: potential outcomes are independent of treatment given the baseline covariates; positivity: both treatment levels have positive probability across the target covariate support; no interference: one unit's treatment does not change another unit's outcome",
